From ad8063ada32002569abea1c7ecced2cf582e7e7c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:27:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Bluetooth: btusb: assume working SCO buffers on the CSR
 clone 0a12:0001 bcdDevice 0x8891 subversion 0x2312

This clone is not told apart from a genuine CSR dongle by the existing
checks, and with the default setup no SCO connection can be made: SCO
MTU 48:0 is logged and every connect is refused. Set
HCI_QUIRK_FIXUP_BUFFER_SIZE, as for the genuine old CSR dongles
(BTUSB_WRONG_SCO_MTU), unless disable_scofix is set.

Whether the clone carries voice is proven only by audio through a real
SCO link, in CVSD and mSBC.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
---
 drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
index 2154ad8..a92e458 100644
--- a/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
+++ b/drivers/bluetooth/btusb.c
@@ -2718,6 +2718,13 @@ static int btusb_setup_csr(struct hci_dev *hdev)
 			usb_enable_autosuspend(data->udev);
 	}
 
+	/* Assume working SCO buffers for this clone (bcdDevice 0x8891, LMP
+	 * subversion 0x2312), as for the genuine old CSR dongles.
+	 */
+	if (bcdDevice == 0x8891 && le16_to_cpu(rp->lmp_subver) == 0x2312 &&
+	    !disable_scofix)
+		hci_set_quirk(hdev, HCI_QUIRK_FIXUP_BUFFER_SIZE);
+
 	kfree_skb(skb);
 
 	return 0;
